 "note": "Web tools worked, but several pages (HHS, USHMM, Hopkins, PubMed, some Wikipedia) returned 403/404 or empty, so those claims are marked unverifiable. Questions answered from knowledge; none found wrong. Euthanasia and abortion positions are presented even-handedly. Additional pages opened and consistent with the course: AMA opposes physician-assisted suicide (https://code-medical-ethics.ama-assn.org/ethics-opinions/physician-assisted-suicide); Netherlands law in force 1 April 2002 (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euthanasia_in_the_Netherlands); Carter v Canada 6 Feb 2015 and Bill C-14 June 2016 (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carter_v_Canada_(Attorney_General)); Belmont three principles, report Sept 1978 and Federal Register April 1979 (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belmont_Report), so the lesson date 1979 is conventional.",
